  "body": "Found by the other session's review of #1158 (2026-11-13). On main, the Wire Contour's **taper** stamp input (added by #1163) is unpinned: replacing its digest write with `if false { ... }` passes every test. So a regression that drops the taper from the stamp would leave a path computed at the old taper marked Ok and postable after the taper is edited.\n\n**Done means:** a test in the wire stamp suite asserts that changing only `taper_deg` (and, if the machine's taper limits feed the stamp, those too) changes the stamp. It is mutation-checked: deleting each digest line turns it red.\n",
